"content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": ""}, {"time": "100", "text": "If you can't sleep, you might want to look at your diet. Research has shown that what and when people eat can be connected to how well they sleep. If you eat a big meal an hour before going to bed, you probably won't sleep well.  The chances of not sleeping are even greater if your meal is more spicy or fatty than usual.", "id": 1, "image": ""}, {"time": "21000", "text": "Another reason that people don't sleep is because they don't eat enough. If you're on a diet, you may have trouble going to sleep. Experts suggest that if you have trouble sleeping, you could try keeping a regular eating schedule during the day and having a light snack at night.", "id": 2, "image": ""}, {"time": "40000", "text": "Alcohol and caffeine can also affect your sleep. If you drink alcohol before you go to sleep, you may fall asleep quickly, but you'll probably sleep lightly. There's also a chance that you'll wake up in the middle of the night. If you have more caffeine late in the day, your sleep will most probably be affected. You should avoid drinking too many caffeinated beverages.", "id": 3, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn7le02ob01re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 2}], "id": 0}]}